From 7dbdd073176fde6dd33dc56de5438c58284e32b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:14:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools: qwen4exp MTP sidecar builders, with Strata's fetch
 tool and its MIT license

The published Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GGUFs carry no MTP head, so nobody outside could build the
sidecar our recipe names. tools/qwen4exp-mtp-sidecar/ ships the full chain: Strata's
mtp_fetch.py (+ its mocked test) fetches the 31 BF16 mtp.* tensors at a pinned Qwen revision,
build_sidecar.py verifies the ashbash Q8_0 head against that BF16 truth and writes the sidecar,
make_dvocab_sidecar.py writes the optional 40,525-token draft-vocabulary head. README pins every
input and gives the sha256 of both outputs. Strata's MIT text joins licenses/ with its row.

Origin: lane-298 (build_sidecar.py, make_dvocab_sidecar.py, README.md)
Taken-from: Niko1221/Strata@82f46a8c8f475f001ad76d92f58f4a4f8ffb0253 (tools/mtp_fetch.py, tools/test_mtp_fetch.py, LICENSE; copied unchanged)
Measured-effect: none on the engine (tools only); the shipped scripts regenerate both served sidecars with identical tensors, cache/mtp-x1-lane/cells/sidecar-regen.txt
